{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And YHWH uprooted them from upon their land</b> — for the tribe that does evil in the eyes of YHWH will be exiled, as in the matter of \"and He exiled them to the Reubenites and the Gadites\" (I Chronicles 5:26). But the correct interpretation is that now He hints at the exile of all Israel, for they will all be evil, and they will go into a complete exile. And so in the section coming after it (Deuteronomy 30:1), \"And it shall be, when all these things come upon you\" — this concerns the exile of all Israel, as He says (ibid.), \"among all the nations where YHWH your Elohim has driven you there,\" and so forth. And the entire section [follows this theme]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:36.637055901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}